Package: orderBookSim
Type: Package
Title: Agent-Based Limit Order Book Simulation for Market Microstructure
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Moses", "Adebayo", , "adebayomoses2021@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Simulates a continuous double-auction limit order book with
    price-time priority matching, driven by configurable populations of
    trading agents: zero-intelligence order flow in the spirit of Smith,
    Farmer, Gillemot and Krishnamurthy (2003) <doi:10.1088/1469-7688/3/6/307>,
    noise traders, inventory-constrained market makers, momentum traders and
    informed traders who observe a latent fundamental value. Exogenous
    liquidity shocks can be injected at chosen events. Tools measure
    time-weighted bid-ask spreads, depth, price impact, resilience after
    shocks and the stylised facts of returns, and an optional 'shiny'
    application lets students explore how agent mixes shape liquidity.
